namespace FamilyQuant;

public static class FamilyListImportHelp
{
    public const string DecisionsSummary = "Quantify, merge, report under others or leave out; no conditional action. Your labels stay with each family.";
    public const string DoneNext = "Next: Group by evidence reads the database and scope by itself when it opens (this takes minutes); then press Update proposal to see the family checklist.";
    public const string MatchingEffect = "Matching labels families; proteins move only when you change the scope or place them by hand, then Apply grouping.";
    public const string Text = "IMPORT FAMILY LIST\n\n"
        + "1. Welcome. Choose an Excel workbook with an abbreviation and name for each family. Use template writes an empty workbook with the program's columns, ready to fill and import. Edit current panel keeps the existing editor available.\n\n"
        + "2. File and sheet. Browse or drop one .xlsx file, choose its family sheet, and check the proposed header row. After editing the row number, press Read this header row. The preview retains source text and row numbers; select a cell and open Cell details for the complete text, fill name and merged range. Workbook colours are data, never decisions; yellow and gold fills are shown neutrally. Other sheets can be ignored or kept as original source notes.\n\n"
        + "3. Columns. Check each column choice and its example. Abbreviation and Family name are required. Other-language name, notes and Pfam are optional, and every original column is retained. Without a Decision column, every family is Quantify, and Next asks you to confirm that choice once for this import. A suggested column of repeated short labels is only a hint; Use this decision column selects it for review, never accepts its actions automatically. When a Decision column uses your own words, review each distinct source value and its rows, edit its action or merge target, and press Confirm these actions.\n\n"
        + "DECISION ACTIONS\n" + DecisionsSummary + " Quantify keeps the family as its own reporting unit; Merge into family uses a chosen target; Report under others keeps one group in others; Not a family leaves it out as a reporting family; its source row remains available. A condition written in your spreadsheet is source text, never an automatic condition. You choose the action now, and the original decision label stays with the imported family.\n\n"
        + "4. Special rows. The source row, problem and proposed correction stay visible. Choose how to handle a row listing several names, a repeated abbreviation or a missing value, then press Use this choice. You may rename, skip or merge a repeated row; a several-name row can become one family per name or one group reported under others. Empty/decorative rows skipped by the reader remain listed. No unresolved row is silently dropped.\n\n"
        + "5. Pfam choices. Codes found in the stored Pfam list are taken directly from your sheet. Only rows written as names or codes not found need a choice, one line per row. Select and confirm their stored-evidence match, or explicitly skip it. A row with no Pfam code is named in Summary and gets no proteins until it has one. Counts are distinct database entries, not abundance; overlapping suggestions must not be added. The wizard uses stored evidence and never downloads it.\n\n"
        + "6. Summary. Review the panel name, families, source notes, actions and matching choices. Import replaces the current panel, if any, as one project edit. Everything before Import is a detached draft; Back keeps your choices, and Cancel changes nothing. Source and project changes are checked again before publication.\n\n"
        + "7. Done. Choose Family checklist to review protein membership separately. " + DoneNext + " " + MatchingEffect + " Import itself leaves grouping and quantitation unchanged. Undo import restores the previous panel while this import remains the current Undo step. Close keeps the imported panel; File > Save persists it in the project.\n\n"
        + "KEYBOARD\nTab follows the controls in reading order; arrows work in native tables and choices. Enter activates the enabled forward action outside a table edit. Escape cancels or closes; F1 opens this Help.\n";
}
